  "methods": ["compound angle formula", "rewriting sin^2 in terms of cos"],
  "statement": "Prove that $\\cos3\\theta=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta$.",
  "solution": "\\begin{align*}\n\\cos3\\theta&=\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\n&=\\cos2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\sin2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\n&=(2\\cos^{2}\\theta-1)\\cos\\theta-2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\n&=2\\cos^{3}\\theta-\\cos\\theta-2\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos^{2}\\theta)\\\\\n&=2\\cos^{3}\\theta-\\cos\\theta-2\\cos\\theta+2\\cos^{3}\\theta\\\\\n&=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta.\n\\end{align*}",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Write cos 3θ = cos(2θ+θ).",
    "Use the double-angle formulas.",
    "Replace sin^2θ by 1 - cos^2θ."
  ]
}
